fact that the derivation of the exact expression for the stability boundaries is possible. However, it is commonly acknowledged that it is at least necessary to consider a 4-dof model (flapping rotor on a pylon with pitch and yaw degree of freedom) to obtain a more appropriate representation, especially when considering a tiltrotor proprotor. A schematic view of this configuration is shown in Fig. 10.
Figure 10: 4-dof Proprotor Model [100]
Also, for this case, which at least overcomes the limitations given by rigid propeller modeling, it may be required to add at least a few more degrees of freedom for both rotor and support in order to obtain meaningful results. Johnson [87] later proposed a theoretical model that provided the ability to investigate the dynamics of the proprotor on a cantilever wing, as shown in Fig. 11.
