DUST is an open-source software designed using object-oriented paradigms of the latest FORTRAN standards. Different classical potential-based elements are implemented in the code, such as lifting line [66, 156], surface panels [133], and linear vortex lattice elements [91] and nonlinear vortex lattice element [39]. Even if incompressible potential flow is considered in the code assumptions, compressibility effects are considered in the computations. In particular, a Prandtl-Glauert correction [103] is considered for the calculation of steady aerodynamic loads with surface panels and vortex lattice elements. On the other hand, lifting line and non-linear vortex lattice elements intrinsically include compressibility and viscous effects introduced by Machdepending tabulated sectional aerodynamic coefficients, obtained by experiments or by 2D RANS numerical simulations. Figure 19 summarizes the typical workflow needed to build and run a DUST model.
