The implemented codes are validated considering several test cases [38, 39, 169, 171]. The first validation is provided by analyzing Goland wing, a numerical test case that was widely used in the literature as a benchmark for flutter predictions. This validated the coupling procedure between DUST and MBDyn. The second groups of test cases are related to the validation of the nonlinear vortex lattice element. Three cases are considered:
