3.3 non-linear vortex lattice
The present section describes the results of the validation of the novel non-linear vortex lattice element tested on both fixed-wing and rotarywing benchmark cases available from the literature for aerodynamic and aeroelastic problems.
3.3.1 Finite Wing
Firstly, a simple finite wing benchmark case is considered to test the correct implementation of the method. In particular, the test case consists of a rectangular wing with an aspect ratio equal to 12, a constant chord of 1 m and a constant NACA4415 airfoil section. Figure 35b shows the comparison of the wing lift coefficient as a function of the angle of attack calculated by high-fidelity CFD simulations by Hosangadi et al. [154] and by DUST using both the LL and VL elements already implemented and the novel non-linear vortex lattice method (NL-VL). The effectiveness of the non-linear vortex-lattice method is evident, as shown by the remarkable agreement with the curves


